flowchart TB
    A["A: Objective<br>Build a sustainable business (money in the bank account)"]
    B["B: Sell what I know is right<br>VSM, flow, WIP management -- DORA-backed, evidence-based"]
    C["C: Sell what people will pay for<br>Whatever the market is actually spending money on right now"]
    D["D: Keep positioning as VSM/flow expert<br>Lead with method, cite DORA, educate the market"]
    Dprime["D': Sell something else entirely<br>Find what people buy, package around that"]

    A --> B
    A --> C
    B --> D
    C --> Dprime
    D <-.->|"CONFLICT"| Dprime

    subgraph assumptions ["Hidden assumptions to challenge"]
        H1["B-D: If research supports it, people will eventually buy"]
        H1a["A year of evidence says they won't. Research is not purchase orders."]
        H2["B-D: I need to educate the market to create demand"]
        H2a["Educating is a 3-5 year play. You need revenue now."]
        H3["C-D': Selling what market buys means abandoning my skills"]
        H3a["Your skills apply to many offerings."]
        H4["C-D': I don't know what the market wants"]
        H4a["This is the real blocker. The demand research answers it."]
    end

    subgraph injection ["Possible injection (UNVALIDATED)"]
        OA["Option A: Repackage VSM as AI-delivery-gap consulting<br>Use DORA data as credibility, sell the pain not the method."]
        OB["Option B: Pivot to DevOps/platform/AI gigs<br>Use technical background to take freelance projects."]
        OC["Option C: Part-time job + part-time Flowtopia<br>Stabilize income, continue building the practice."]
    end

    WARNING{{"All three options require the same first step:<br>find out what the market is actually spending on"}}

    Dprime -.-> injection
    injection --> WARNING

